Q. Given a square chessboard of n x n size, the position of the knight and the position of a target are given and
we need to find out the minimum steps a knight will take to reach the target position.

Example 1:-
knight position : (1,3)
target position : (5,0)
output : 3
(1,3) to (5,0)
steps : (1,3) -> (3,4) -> (4,2) -> (5,0)

Approach:
Use BFS on Graph
Note: DP solution is not possible as you would end up visiting same cells again. Hence, Graph approach provides a natural way of maintaining
a visited array and solving this problem.